  "body": "I have difficulties understanding [Focus fixup rule one](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focus-fixup-rule-one). My simplified interpretation is »in case the focused element is no longer focusable, the first focusable element in that document should receive focus.«\r\n\r\nI've run a [simple test](https://jsbin.com/fesexin/) mutating the active element so that it isn't focusable anymore and [the results](https://allyjs.io/tutorials/mutating-active-element.html#the-results) are quite uniform, but _far_ away from the interpretation of focus fixup rule one.\r\n\r\nIn IRC @zcorpan agreed with my interpretation and raised the question if the specification should be altered to reflect reality.\r\n",
